-- title:
--   Level-M' laws for traces along an Igusa branch
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$.
--
--   **Reduction data at $q$ (`A`, `hA`, `W`, `hW`, `R₀`, `hR₀`, `s`).** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over the residue field of $A$, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map to the residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})$ lies in `ssJSet q`, the set of $j$-values all of whose elliptic models have trivial $q$-torsion. $R₀$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' = \overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the characteristic-zero field, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the characteristic-$q$ field whose kernel is the maximal ideal of `R₀.integers`, and a map on places, subject to the axioms of that structure (contraction of `integers` to $A$ on constants, compatibility of the residue map with the residue map of $A$, the scaling normalisation `exists_smul_mem`, preservation of degrees of places, and compatibility of `placeMap` with orders of functions). The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its $R₀$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$, i.e. a supersingular place of the special fibre.
--
--   **The base field and its uniformiser (`k₀`, `π₀`, `hπ`, `hdvr`, `hunif`).** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$, the contraction $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring, and its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$.
--
--   **The auxiliary level and its function field (`H₁`, `hH₁`, `Kℓ`, `hKℓ`, `jℓ`, `hjℓ`).** $H_1$ is a subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ required to equal $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M' \sqcap \ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times\bigr)$, where $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; thus $H_1$ is the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$. $K_\ell$ is an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ required to equal $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0\,(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,H_1)$, the field generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$; it carries an algebra structure over $A \cap k_0$ compatible with the tower through $k_0$. The element $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ has underlying Laurent series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,\mathrm{jq}$ and is nonzero.
--
--   **The chart and the point $y$ (`y`, `hy`, `hϖy`, `hss`).** $y$ is a maximal ideal of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,(A\cap k_0)\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$, the subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $(A\cap k_0)[j_\ell]$; the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $y$, so $y$ is a point of the special fibre. The hypothesis `hss` says that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, i.e. $y$ is a supersingular point.
--
--   **Compatibility of the chart with the place $s$ (`hover`).** For every $g \in \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose base change lies in `R₀.integers`, which is regular at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which $\mathrm{jq}$ is regular (that is, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the base change of $\mathrm{jq}$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the base change of $g$), whose $R₀$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and such that $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g$ lies in $K_\ell$ and in the chart algebra: for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose $A$-residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R₀$-residue of $g$, the difference of the chart element of $g$ and the image of $c$ lies in $y$.
--
--   **The Igusa parameter (`hjK`, `hjC`, `a₀`, `ha₀y`, `hVj`).** The series $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q$, the $q$-fold $q$-expansion substitution applied to $\mathrm{jqModC}\,k_0$, lies in $K_\ell$ and in the chart algebra; $a_0 \in A\cap k_0$ is such that the corresponding chart element minus $a_0$ lies in $y$. The hypothesis `hVj` is a residual-transcendence condition: for every polynomial $p$ over $A\cap k_0$, if the value at $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q$ of the polynomial obtained by mapping the coefficients into $k_0$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$, then every coefficient of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A\cap k_0$.
--
--   **The Galois data (`ξ`, `hξ`, `G`, `hGatt`, `K₀`, `hK₀`).** $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity. $G$ is a subgroup of the $k_0$-automorphism group of $K_\ell$ such that every $\tau \in G$ is realised by a matrix: there is $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ for which $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,q\,\xi\,q\,(q^2M')\,H_1\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$ holds, i.e. $\tau$ acts on quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ by the slash action of the matrix $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, under any embedding of $k_0$ into $\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ in $K_\ell$.
--
--   **Ends and the Igusa branch (`Wt`, `hR3d`, `Õ`, `hCO`, `hOW`, `O`, `hOdef`, `Wx`, `hOWx`, `hCWx`, `hVA`, `hcentre`, `hne`).** $W_t$ is a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ whose maximal ideal cuts out $y$ on the chart algebra: an element $b$ of the chart algebra lies in $y$ precisely when $b \in W_t$ and $b$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_t$. $\tilde O$ is a subring of $K_\ell$ containing the chart algebra and contained in $W_t$, and $O$ is its preimage in $K_0$. $W_x$ is a further valuation subring of $K_\ell$ containing $\tilde O$ and the chart algebra, prolonging $A \cap k_0$ in the sense that an element of $k_0$ has image in $W_x$ exactly when it comes from $A \cap k_0$ (`hVA`); any element of the chart algebra lying in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ lies in $y$ (`hcentre`), while some element of the chart algebra lies in $y$ but not in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ (`hne`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $g \in \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb Q$ with $g \in \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$, with base change lying in `R₀.integers`, regular at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which the base change of $\mathrm{jq}$ is regular, and with $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g \in K_\ell$, the element $g^\sharp := \langle \mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g\rangle$ of $K_\ell$ lies in the fixed field $K_0$, and, viewed in $K_0$:
--
--   1. $g^\sharp$ lies in the contraction $W_x \cap K_0$ of $W_x$ along $K_0 \to K_\ell$;
--
--   2. $g^\sharp$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x \cap K_0$ if and only if the $R₀$-residue of $g$ is $0$;
--
--   3. if the $R₀$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then $g^\sharp$ lies in $O$ and, for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ and with image in $O$ such that the $A$-residue of $c$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R₀$-residue of $g$, the difference $g^\sharp - c$ is not a unit of $O$.
--
--   This is the node-descent step at a supersingular point: it transfers the level-$M'$ modular functions, their vanishing and their values at a supersingular place $s$ of the characteristic-$q$ modular curve to the fixed field $K_0$ of the Galois group attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ inside the auxiliary field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, measured along an Igusa-type valuation ring $W_x$. It is used by the two per-node trace conclusions for the residual characteristics $q = 2$ and $q = 3$.
